+# Attempt record
+
+Aim: use the new Zeta/Fabel inverse at the actual original ES source, and seek an
+arithmetic return without losing scale, chart signs, prime valuations or positivity.
+
+Read: the pinned GF1-GF28/FC32-FC55 calculation. Its inverse is over the stated
+complex polynomial source; it does not claim arithmetic ES occupancy.
+
+Tested connection: embed the actual three reciprocal roots and infinity in the
+existing quartic target, with coefficient U^3V exactly one. This works with full
+inverse formulas. The original character relations force ramified versus
+unramified factors at p. A preliminary coarse square-class split would have
+allowed seven rational M points, but the exact r/s character relation excludes
+that alternative. It is excluded by proof, not by a search heuristic.
+
+Further mechanism: the root orders have different integral index and conductor.
+Their unique labelled root interpolation supplies an exact rational map and an
+integral reverse, with the obligatory p-denominator calculated. The complex
+conductor and this arithmetic order conductor are explicitly different objects.
+
+Original arithmetic progress: negative-four-square shapes with the proved bounded
+square-divisor availability map to M at the same p. The entire lines alpha=-4
+and beta=-4 are covered without a shape-radius bound. Actual examples with c>1
+and an exhausted blocked source are retained.
+
+Stopping point: the Fabel target is constructed from an existing ES state. Its
+nonempty inverse cannot create that initial state. The arithmetic transfer removes
+branches of the E-only problem but does not make all remaining coefficients
+positive. The universal Turn7 milestone remains unproved.
+
+Attribution: the Fabel polynomial, global inverse and weighted-conductor
+conjugacy are inherited from the cited workbench, not rediscovered here.
+The classical Type-I/II parametrizations and local-field facts are credited.
+No historical priority claim is made for the new arithmetic specialization.
